# Wi-Fi / networking essentials.
# IMPORTANT: the build uses --apt-recommends false, so packages normally pulled
# as Recommends (wpasupplicant, regdb, firmware) must be listed EXPLICITLY, or
# NetworkManager cannot operate Wi-Fi and the adapter looks "not recognized".
wpasupplicant
wireless-regdb
rfkill
iw
wireless-tools
# Broad Wi-Fi firmware coverage for common laptop chipsets (Intel/Atheros/
# Realtek already listed in 00-system; add Broadcom and TI here).
firmware-brcm80211
firmware-iwlwifi
firmware-atheros
firmware-realtek
firmware-ti-connectivity
# ModemManager off by default is fine; NM handles Wi-Fi with wpasupplicant.
